{"_id":"school0000000000000001","name":"Togashi Tattooed Order","type":"school","img":"systems/l5r4-enhanced/assets/icons/school.webp","system":{"description":"<p>Mystical monks with divine tattoos granting supernatural abilities. Unarmed combat specialists.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Benefit:</strong> +1 Void</p>\n<p><strong>Skills:</strong> Athletics, Defense, Craft: Tattooing, Jiujutsu, Any one Lore Skill, Meditation, any one non-Low Skill</p>\n<p><strong>Honor:</strong> 4.5</p>\n<p><strong>Outfit:</strong> Robes, Bo, Traveling Pack, 5 koku</p>\n\n<p>[CR p.112-116]</p>","specialRules":"<h4>RANK 1: BLOOD OF THE KAMI</h4>\n<p>Divine tattoos grant supernatural powers. Gain two Tattoos at this rank.</p>\n\n<h4>RANK 2: BODY OF STONE</h4>\n<p>Mastery of martial arts. +1k1 to all unarmed attack and damage rolls.</p>\n\n<h4>RANK 3: BLESSING OF THE KAMI</h4>\n<p>Continued journey of self-discovery. Gain two additional Tattoos.</p>\n\n<h4>RANK 4: WILL OF STONE</h4>\n<p>Perfect mastery of the flesh. Make unarmed attacks as Simple Action instead of Complex Action.</p>\n\n<h4>RANK 5: TOUCH OF THE KAMI</h4>\n<p>Insight into the true nature of the universe. Gain two additional Tattoos.</p>\n\n<p>Dragon Clan monastic order. Tattoos activate as Free Actions, only one active at a time, effects last rounds equal to 2x School Rank. Tattoos must be exposed (not covered by armor/cloth).</p>\n\n<p><strong>TATTOO NOTES:</strong> Ise zumi gain tattoos at Ranks 1, 3, and 5 (2 tattoos each rank = 6 total). Common tattoos include: Balance, Bamboo, Blaze, Centipede, Crab, Crane, Dragon, Hawk, Ki-Rin, Lion, Mantis (passive), Mountain, Ocean, Phoenix, Scorpion, Spider, Storm, Void, Wind, Wolf. See Dragon Clan source for full tattoo descriptions.</p>","freeRaises":0},"effects":[],"folder":"L5R4 Enhanced/Schools/Dragon/Monk","sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
